Subject: Security audit findings - password hashing
Date: Mon, 14 Apr 2026 09:15:00 +0200
Message-ID: <audit-001@example.com>

Hi team,

After reviewing the authentication module, I have the following findings:

1. The hash_password function in auth.py uses SHA256 with a static salt.
   This should be migrated to bcrypt or argon2 for production use.
   The current implementation at line 14 concatenates salt + password,
   which is vulnerable to length extension attacks.

2. The verify_password function relies on hash_password internally,
   so fixing the hashing will automatically fix verification.

3. generate_jwt_token uses a hardcoded secret key ('demo-jwt-secret').
   This must be replaced with an environment variable before deployment.

4. The require_auth middleware decorator correctly validates tokens via
   verify_jwt_token, but does not check token expiration robustly.

Please prioritize these fixes before the next release.

Best regards,
Security Team
